# =============================================================================
# AMSC_STFT — everything that is produced, never authored.
#
# The rule of thumb: if a command creates it, it belongs here. Build trees,
# benchmark output, parsed CSVs, figures and generated audio are all
# reproducible from the sources, and keeping them out of the repository is what
# makes a fresh clone small enough to read.
# =============================================================================

# ── Build trees ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
bin/
lib/
out/
.cmake/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
compile_commands.json

# ── Object files, libraries, executables ─────────────────────────────────────
*.d
*.slo
*.lo
*.o
*.obj
*.su
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib

# ── Everything a run produces ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One tree, so one rule covers it. Each subdirectory is named after what
# writes to it:
#     results/results_benchmark/  run_suite.sh: benchmark CSVs, environment log
#     results/results_test/       run_suite.sh: ctest log and working copy
#     results/results_analysis/   parse_results.py + plot_results.py output
#     results/results_examples/   the spectrograms the two examples write
results/
tmp/

# Older layouts and stray overrides, kept so a run that predates the tree above
# — or one pointed elsewhere with -o / --out — cannot be committed by accident.
results-*/
benchmark-results*/
csv/
plots/
raw/
analysis/csv/
analysis/figures/
ctest-run/

# SLURM / PBS job logs
*.out
*.err
amsc_stft_job.*

# ── Personal cluster submission scripts ─────────────────────────────────────
# Tied to one person's HPC account (project code, home/work paths, access and
# toolchain details for CINECA and MOX). Two files in scripts/ are meant to be
# public: run_suite.sh (the actual benchmark recipe) and job.sh (the small,
# account-free entry point the CI/CD pipeline submits). Everything else there
# — job_full.sh and any cluster-specific helper — is a private script and
# ignored by default, so a new one added later does not need to be remembered
# here too.
scripts/*
!scripts/run_suite.sh
!scripts/job.sh

# ── Generated media ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spectrograms and the audio the examples and tests synthesise.
*.ppm
*.png
*.mp3
*.wav
# ...except everything under core/examples/data/. Those are inputs, not output:
# the examples analyse them, and test_WavReader reads test_audio.wav — without
# it that test does not fail, it silently skips, which is worse. The four demo
# signals are regenerated exactly by scripts/make_demo_audio.py, but are kept in
# the tree so that a fresh clone can run the examples straight away.
!core/examples/data/*.wav

# ...and except the figures used by the report, which are spectrograms produced
# by the examples and then re-encoded by analysis/prepare_figures.py. They are
# checked in because reproducing them means building the project first.
!docs/figures/*.png

# ── Generated documentation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Doxyfile is committed; the HTML it produces is regenerated on demand.
docs/doxygen/

# ── Containers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sif

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ── Editors and local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.kdev4
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
